# Agent worktrees. The monorepo's own .gitignore covers these, but it does not travel:
# this repository is produced by `git subtree split`, which carries only this folder.
#
# Note that git is not the real safeguard here. RimWorld's Workshop uploader calls
# SteamUGC.SetItemContent on the folder the junction points at and sends it whole, with no
# filtering: it never reads a .gitignore, so anything dropped in the published folder ships.
# What protects the publication is the split itself - only Mod/ is published, and the
# junction in RimWorld\Mods points at Mod/, never at this root.
.claude/

# Build output. Directory.Build.props sends intermediates outside the mod folder entirely;
# these entries are the safety net if that ever stops holding.
.build/
obj/
bin/
.vs/
*.user
